pub fn score(&self) -> Option<u16> {
    if self.frames.len() < 10 { return None; }
    let tenth = &self.frames[9];
    let complete = match tenth.len() {
        2 => tenth[0] + tenth[1] < 10,
        3 => true,
        _ => false,
    };
    if !complete { return None; }
    // flatten
    let rolls: Vec<u16> = self.frames.iter().flatten().copied().collect();
    let mut total = 0;
    let mut i = 0;
    for f in 0..10 {
        if rolls[i] == 10 {
            total += 10 + rolls[i+1] + rolls[i+2];
            i += 1;
        } else if i + 1 < rolls.len() && rolls[i] + rolls[i+1] == 10 {
            total += 10 + rolls[i+2];
            i += 2;
        } else {
            total += rolls[i] + rolls[i+1];
            i += 2;
        }
    }
    Some(total)
}
```

Wait — for a spare in the 10th frame: rolls[i]+rolls[i+1]==10, and rolls[i+2] exists (the bonus ball). No problem. For a strike in the 10th frame: rolls[i]==10, and i+1, i+2 exist. No problem.

Note: for a spare in the 10th frame, the "10 + next roll" rule is fine because the next roll is the bonus ball that gets counted only once.

Edge case: in frames 1–9, a spare is always followed by at least one more roll, so rolls[i+2] exists. Good.

